t-dj-jacobs-commits-miami-hours-decommitting-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"D.J. Jacobs decommits from Ohio State, sources say, making top DE available again","description":"D.J. Jacobs, the No. 2 overall recruit in the 2027 class, has decommitted from Ohio State, sources told ESPN, with Tennessee, Georgia and Miami among the leading contenders for the five-star defensive end.","published":"2026-11-26T21:21:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50606035/sources-de-dj-jacobs-decommits-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Friday Night Lights,' 'Ted Lasso' top poll ranking 21st-century sports shows","description":"A Seton Hall poll crowns America's favorite modern fictional sports TV series.﻿","published":"2026-11-26T16:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50576889/top-fictional-sports-series-21st-century","type":"Story","byline":"Brianna Williams","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"The oldest grudge in football","description":"When Texas Tech and its brash benefactor bought their way into the college football big time, they were settling an old West Texas score.","published":"2026-11-26T13:12:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50427039/texas-tech-puf-cody-campbell","type":"Story","byline":"Dave Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-26T13:09:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"USC band won't perform at UCLA football game after members vandalized campus","description":"The USC Trojan Marching Band will not perform during Saturday's rivalry game against UCLA after members of the band vandalized a portion of UCLA's campus.","published":"2026-11-26T14:39:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50600615/usc-band-perform-members-vandalized-ucla-campus","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kent State TD overturned by replay was incorrect decision, MAC says","description":"A Kent State touchdown catch should not have been overturned by replay to incomplete at the end of Tuesday's 17-12 loss to Eastern Michigan, the Mid-American Conference said Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T23:05:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50597875/kent-state-td-overturned-replay-was-incorrect-mac-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5121819/luke-talich","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luke_Talich"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Luke Talich","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luke_Talich","description":"American football safety (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-23T21:13:02Z","intro":"Lucas Wayne Talich (born July 7, 2004) is an American college football safety for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Talich grew up in Cody, Wyoming and attended Cody High School, where he played basketball and football and competed in track and field. As Cody's starting quarterback during his senior year, he passed for 1,682 yards while also rushing for 582 yards and accounted for 25 touchdowns. Talich was rated a three-star recruit and the top college prospect in Wyoming. He committed to play college football as a preferred walk-on for Notre Dame over scholarship offers from Washington State, Utah, and Wyoming."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Talich initially intended on redshirting his true freshman season at the University of Notre Dame, but due to injuries on defense and special teams played in the first eight games of the season before suffering a broken collarbone. He was awarded a scholarship during spring practices. Talich returned an interception 79 yards for a touchdown against Florida State during his sophomore year."}]}}